@*
    The avatar editor: a live preview, a radio group of choice cards, and the background swatches. The cards, top to
    bottom, each with a small avatar showing what that choice gives:
      Initials of the name - nothing more.
      A short label        - the label field with its counter, always rendered; typing in it chooses this card.
      Image from the library (only when a library is configured) - a "Choose from library" button. It is not selectable
                  until it holds a picture (its radio input is disabled, so the arrow keys skip it, and a press on the card
                  does nothing); only the button opens the library, and cancelling leaves the earlier choice. Once it holds a picture it
                  shows "Remove image", which returns the choice to Initials since this card cannot be chosen empty.
      Upload an image      - the "Upload…" button. This card can be chosen with no image (the avatar falls back to
                  initials), and "Remove image" keeps it chosen. An avatar with nothing stored opens here, and a stored
                  image always belongs to this card: the saved avatar does not record where it came from.
    There is one image slot (the stored name, or the pending bytes) and a field saying which card owns it; a pick from one
    image card replaces the picture the other held. Each card is a label around a visually hidden radio input (as the
    swatches are), so Tab reaches the group and the arrow keys move within it; a click on empty card space chooses it, and
    choosing is idempotent because the label, the input and the card all report one press. It is one component
    for every surface that edits an Avatar, so the rules live once: the label is trimmed through Avatar.TrimLabel, an
    upload is checked against AvatarImage.MaxBytes and then AvatarImage.SniffExtension, and a background is only ever set
    by pressing a swatch.

    SaveMode says who writes:
      Immediate - every change is written to the AvatarStore under Name at once (the Settings page, which has no Save
                  button); a chosen image is written through AvatarStore.WriteImage.
      Buffered  - nothing is written. Each change is reported through ValueChanged, and a chosen image's bytes and
                  extension through PendingImageChanged, for the surface that owns the Save button to write (or drop).
                  Leaving an image card for a card that does not own the image, or pressing Remove image, drops the
                  pending image (null, null) so a surface never files an orphan.

    Value is the avatar to start from and is read as a snapshot: the editor re-seeds only when the parent passes a Value
    that differs from the last one it passed AND from what the editor already holds. That second test is the echo guard.
    Choosing "A short label" before typing saves Avatar.None; the parent then hands back Avatar.None, and re-seeding from
    it would snap the choice back to Initials - the very choice the Human just made, undone by its own save.

    THE BACKGROUND: "no background chosen" is null, and the background changes only in OnBackgroundPickedAsync, which
    only a press on a swatch reaches, so nothing is written on first render (docs/engineering/traps.md). The swatches
    are a radio group of 32px circles drawn with the avatar recipe for the current mode (audit B8h), one per
    AvatarPalette.Swatches entry, the same set a new Agent's random colour is drawn from, each with its colour name.
    A stored colour outside the palette highlights no swatch and is kept until one is pressed. A background sits behind
    initials or a label; an image covers it, so under either image card the swatches are not offered - the stored colour
    is left alone.

    The library (audit B8k): "Choose from library" opens the Avatar Library. Outside a dialog (Settings) that is a dialog
    of its own. Inside one (the Agent card's avatar dialog) a third dialog would stack three deep, so the library
    replaces the editor's content in the same dialog, with a Back button, and the dialog is widened to the library's
    width meanwhile; the editor's working state stays in this component's fields, so Back returns to it untouched.
    LibraryOpenChanged tells the hosting dialog so it can retitle itself and hide its own buttons.

    Parameter types must not be internal (CS0053), so the choice itself is a private field of the internal AvatarChoice.
*@

@using Agency.Huddle.App.Avatars
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Forms
@using Agency.Huddle.App.Themes
@inject AvatarStore Avatars
@inject IDialogService DialogService
@inject AvatarLibraryLocator LibraryLocator
@inject IAvatarLibraryLoader LibraryLoader

@if (this.libraryOpen)
{
    <div class="avatar-library-inline">
        <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Size="Size.Small" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ArrowBack" OnClick="this.CloseLibraryAsync" Class="avatar-library-back mb-2">Back</MudButton>
        <AvatarLibraryPicker OnPicked="this.OnLibraryPickedAsync" OnCancel="this.CloseLibraryAsync" />
    </div>
}
else
{
<div class="avatar-editor">
    <MudStack Row="true" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Class="mb-2">
        <AgentAvatar Name="@this.Name" Avatar="this.Working" Size="Size.Large"
                        PendingImage="this.pendingBytes" PendingImageExtension="@this.pendingExtension" />
    </MudStack>

    <div class="avatar-choices" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Avatar">
        <div class="@this.CardClass(AvatarChoice.Initials)" @onclick="@(() => this.ChooseAsync(AvatarChoice.Initials))">
            <label class="avatar-choice-pick">
                <input type="radio" name="avatar-choice" class="visually-hidden"
                       checked="@(this.choice == AvatarChoice.Initials)" @onclick="@(() => this.ChooseAsync(AvatarChoice.Initials))" />
                <AgentAvatar Name="@this.Name" Avatar="this.InitialsThumb" Size="Size.Medium" />
                <span class="avatar-choice-title">Initials of the name</span>
            </label>
        </div>

        <div class="@this.CardClass(AvatarChoice.Label)" @onclick="@(() => this.ChooseAsync(AvatarChoice.Label))">
            <label class="avatar-choice-pick">
                <input type="radio" name="avatar-choice" class="visually-hidden"
                       checked="@(this.choice == AvatarChoice.Label)" @onclick="@(() => this.ChooseAsync(AvatarChoice.Label))" />
                <AgentAvatar Name="@this.Name" Avatar="this.LabelThumb" Size="Size.Medium" />
                <span class="avatar-choice-title">A short label</span>
            </label>
            <div class="avatar-choice-body">
                @* No MaxLength: it truncates by UTF-16 index, which can cut a surrogate pair in half. Counter gives the same
                   affordance without that defect, sized from Avatar.MaxLabelTextElements so the two can never drift apart.
                   Trimming happens once, in Working's Avatar.TrimLabel call, not here. *@
                <MudTextField T="string" Label="Label" Variant="Variant.Outlined" Margin="Margin.Dense"
                              Value="@this.label" ValueChanged="this.OnLabelChangedAsync"
                              Immediate="true" Counter="@Avatar.MaxLabelTextElements" />
            </div>
        </div>

        @if (this.LibraryLocator.IsConfigured)
        {
            <div class="@this.CardClass(AvatarChoice.Library)" @onclick="@(() => this.ChooseAsync(AvatarChoice.Library))">
                <label class="avatar-choice-pick">
                    <input type="radio" name="avatar-choice" class="visually-hidden"
                           checked="@(this.choice == AvatarChoice.Library)" disabled="@(!this.LibraryHoldsImage)"
                           @onclick="@(() => this.ChooseAsync(AvatarChoice.Library))" />
                    <AgentAvatar Name="@this.Name" Avatar="this.LibraryThumb" Size="Size.Medium"
                                 PendingImage="this.LibraryHoldsImage ? this.pendingBytes : null"
                                 PendingImageExtension="@(this.LibraryHoldsImage ? this.pendingExtension : null)" />
                    <span class="avatar-choice-title">Image from the library</span>
                </label>
                <div class="avatar-choice-body">
                    <span class="avatar-choice-actions" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                        <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" Size="Size.Small" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.PhotoLibrary" OnClick="this.ChooseFromLibraryAsync">
                            Choose from library
                        </MudButton>
                    </span>
                    @if (this.LibraryHoldsImage)
                    {
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">@this.HeldImageText</MudText>
                        <span class="avatar-choice-actions" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                            <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Size="Size.Small" OnClick="this.RemoveImageAsync">Remove image</MudButton>
                        </span>
                    }
                </div>
            </div>
        }

        <div class="@this.CardClass(AvatarChoice.Upload)" @onclick="@(() => this.ChooseAsync(AvatarChoice.Upload))">
            <label class="avatar-choice-pick">
                <input type="radio" name="avatar-choice" class="visually-hidden"
                       checked="@(this.choice == AvatarChoice.Upload)" @onclick="@(() => this.ChooseAsync(AvatarChoice.Upload))" />
                <AgentAvatar Name="@this.Name" Avatar="this.UploadThumb" Size="Size.Medium"
                             PendingImage="this.UploadHoldsImage ? this.pendingBytes : null"
                             PendingImageExtension="@(this.UploadHoldsImage ? this.pendingExtension : null)" />
                <span class="avatar-choice-title">Upload an image</span>
            </label>
            <div class="avatar-choice-body">
                <span class="avatar-choice-actions" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                    <MudFileUpload T="IBrowserFile" Accept=".png,.jpg,.jpeg,.webp" MaximumFileCount="1" FilesChanged="this.OnFileChangedAsync">
                        <CustomContent Context="fileUpload">
                            <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" Size="Size.Small" StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Upload" OnClick="@(() => fileUpload.OpenFilePickerAsync())">
                                Upload…
                            </MudButton>
                        </CustomContent>
                    </MudFileUpload>
                </span>
                @if (this.UploadHoldsImage)
                {
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">@this.HeldImageText</MudText>
                    <span class="avatar-choice-actions" @onclick:stopPropagation="true">
                        <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Size="Size.Small" OnClick="this.RemoveImageAsync">Remove image</MudButton>
                    </span>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    @if (this.error is not null)
    {
        <MudAlert Severity="Severity.Error" Dense="true" Class="mt-2" role="alert">@this.error</MudAlert>
    }

    @* Under an image card the Background is hidden, not removed: it keeps its space, so the dialog does not change height
       and re-centre under the pointer when the Human moves between cards (B8i). inert takes it out of the tab order and
       the accessibility tree. *@
    <div class="@(this.IsImageChoice ? "avatar-editor-background avatar-editor-background-hidden mt-2" : "avatar-editor-background mt-2")"
         inert="@this.IsImageChoice" aria-hidden="@(this.IsImageChoice ? "true" : null)">
        <div class="group-label" id="avatar-editor-background-label">Background</div>
        <div class="avatar-swatches" role="radiogroup" aria-labelledby="avatar-editor-background-label">
            @foreach (AvatarSwatch swatch in AvatarPalette.Swatches)
            {
                <label class="avatar-swatch" title="@swatch.Name">
                    <input type="radio" name="avatar-background" class="avatar-swatch-input visually-hidden"
                           checked="@this.IsChosen(swatch)" @onclick="@(() => this.OnBackgroundPickedAsync(swatch.Hex))" />
                    <span class="avatar-swatch-dot" style="@AvatarColours.MonogramStyle(swatch.Hex)" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                    <span class="visually-hidden">@swatch.Name</span>
                </label>
            }
        </div>
        @if (this.background is not null)
        {
            <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text" Size="Size.Small" OnClick="this.UseThemeColourAsync" Class="mt-1">Use the theme colour</MudButton>
        }
    </div>
</div>
}

@code {
    private AvatarChoice choice;
    private string label = string.Empty;
    private string? image;
    private string? background;
    private string? error;
    private byte[]? pendingBytes;
    private string? pendingExtension;
    private Avatar lastValue = Avatar.None;
    private bool libraryOpen;
    private bool imageFromLibrary;

    [CascadingParameter]
    private IMudDialogInstance? Dialog { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The Name the avatar belongs to: the initials source for the preview and, in <see cref="AvatarSaveMode.Immediate"/>, the key the avatar is saved under.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The avatar to edit: what is stored, or what the owning surface currently holds. A different value from the last one passed, and from what the editor already holds, re-seeds the editor.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Avatar Value { get; set; } = Avatar.None;

    /// <summary>Raised with the working avatar after every change, once it has been written in <see cref="AvatarSaveMode.Immediate"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<Avatar> ValueChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether changes are written at once or only reported.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public AvatarSaveMode SaveMode { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Bytes of an image chosen earlier and not yet written, used to seed a <see cref="AvatarSaveMode.Buffered"/> editor on its first render.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public byte[]? PendingImage { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The extension, with its dot, of <see cref="PendingImage"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? PendingImageExtension { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised in <see cref="AvatarSaveMode.Buffered"/> when an image is chosen (bytes and extension) or dropped (both null).</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<(byte[]? Bytes, string? Extension)> PendingImageChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Raised with true when the library replaces the editor's content inside a dialog, and false when Back brings the editor back, so the hosting dialog can retitle itself and hide its own buttons.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<bool> LibraryOpenChanged { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The single place the editor's fields are projected back into an <see cref="Avatar"/>: for the preview and for everything reported or saved. Under the image card that owns the slot, the stored name only, never a pending one.</summary>
    private Avatar Working => new(
        this.choice == AvatarChoice.Label ? Avatar.TrimLabel(this.label) : null,
        this.OwnsImageSlot(this.choice) ? this.image : null,
        this.background);

    /// <summary>Whether the chosen card is an image card (library or upload), which hides the Background swatches.</summary>
    private bool IsImageChoice => this.choice is AvatarChoice.Library or AvatarChoice.Upload;

    /// <summary>Whether the single image slot holds a picture, stored or pending.</summary>
    private bool HasImage => this.image is not null || this.pendingBytes is not null;

    /// <summary>Whether the library card holds the picture: it is selectable only then.</summary>
    private bool LibraryHoldsImage => this.imageFromLibrary && this.HasImage;

    /// <summary>Whether the upload card holds the picture. A stored image on reopen always belongs here: the saved avatar does not record where it came from.</summary>
    private bool UploadHoldsImage => !this.imageFromLibrary && this.HasImage;

    /// <summary>The thumbnail of the Initials card: the initials with the current background.</summary>
    private Avatar InitialsThumb => new(null, null, this.background);

    /// <summary>The thumbnail of the Label card: the trimmed label, or the initials while it is empty.</summary>
    private Avatar LabelThumb => new(Avatar.TrimLabel(this.label), null, this.background);

    /// <summary>The thumbnail of the library card: its picture, or the initials while it holds none.</summary>
    private Avatar LibraryThumb => new(null, this.LibraryHoldsImage ? this.image : null, this.background);

    /// <summary>The thumbnail of the upload card: its picture, or the initials while it holds none.</summary>
    private Avatar UploadThumb => new(null, this.UploadHoldsImage ? this.image : null, this.background);

    /// <summary>What an image card says about the picture it holds: the pending note, or the stored file name.</summary>
    private string? HeldImageText => this.pendingBytes is not null ? "New image selected (not yet saved)" : this.image;

    /// <summary>Whether <paramref name="value"/> is an image card that owns the image slot, so that choosing it makes the avatar's image the slot's.</summary>
    /// <param name="value">The card to test.</param>
    private bool OwnsImageSlot(AvatarChoice value) => value switch
    {
        AvatarChoice.Library => this.imageFromLibrary,
        AvatarChoice.Upload => !this.imageFromLibrary,
        _ => false,
    };

    /// <summary>The CSS class of a choice card, marking the chosen one.</summary>
    /// <param name="value">The card.</param>
    private string CardClass(AvatarChoice value) =>
        this.choice == value ? "avatar-choice-card avatar-choice-card-selected" : "avatar-choice-card";

    /// <summary>Whether <paramref name="swatch"/> is the chosen background. A background outside the palette matches none and is kept until a swatch is pressed.</summary>
    /// <param name="swatch">The swatch to test.</param>
    private bool IsChosen(AvatarSwatch swatch) => string.Equals(this.background, swatch.Hex, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);

    /// <summary>Seeds the editor from <see cref="Value"/> and, once, from the pending-image parameters.</summary>
    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        this.Seed(this.Value);
        this.lastValue = this.Value;
        if (this.PendingImage is not null && this.PendingImageExtension is not null)
        {
            this.pendingBytes = this.PendingImage;
            this.pendingExtension = this.PendingImageExtension;
            this.choice = AvatarChoice.Upload;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Re-seeds only for a genuinely new <see cref="Value"/> - see the file-level comment for the echo guard.</summary>
    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (this.Value == this.lastValue)
        {
            return;
        }

        this.lastValue = this.Value;
        if (this.Value != this.Working)
        {
            this.Seed(this.Value);
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Sets every field from <paramref name="avatar"/>, deriving the choice from which of image and label is set - the precedence <see cref="AgentAvatar"/> renders by - and dropping any pending image and error. A stored image, and an avatar with nothing stored, belong to the upload card.</summary>
    /// <param name="avatar">The avatar to show.</param>
    private void Seed(Avatar avatar)
    {
        this.choice = avatar switch
        {
            { Image: not null } => AvatarChoice.Upload,
            { Label: not null } => AvatarChoice.Label,
            _ => AvatarChoice.Upload,
        };
        this.imageFromLibrary = false;
        this.label = avatar.Label ?? string.Empty;
        this.image = avatar.Image;
        this.background = avatar.Background;
        this.pendingBytes = null;
        this.pendingExtension = null;
        this.error = null;
    }

    /// <summary>Writes <see cref="Working"/> under <see cref="Name"/> in <see cref="AvatarSaveMode.Immediate"/>, then reports it.</summary>
    private async Task CommitAsync()
    {
        Avatar working = this.Working;
        if (this.SaveMode == AvatarSaveMode.Immediate)
        {
            this.Avatars.Save(this.Name, working);
        }

        await this.ValueChanged.InvokeAsync(working);
    }

    /// <summary>Drops a pending image and tells the parent, when there is one.</summary>
    private async Task DropPendingAsync()
    {
        if (this.pendingBytes is null)
        {
            return;
        }

        this.pendingBytes = null;
        this.pendingExtension = null;
        await this.PendingImageChanged.InvokeAsync((null, null));
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Chooses a card. Idempotent: a label click, the input's click and the card's own click all arrive for one press, and
    /// only the first changes anything. The library card holds no picture until one is picked, so a press on it then does
    /// nothing: only its "Choose from library" button opens the library.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="value">The card pressed.</param>
    private async Task ChooseAsync(AvatarChoice value)
    {
        if (value == this.choice || (value == AvatarChoice.Library && !this.LibraryHoldsImage))
        {
            return;
        }

        await this.ApplyChoiceAsync(value);
        await this.CommitAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>Makes <paramref name="value"/> the chosen card and clears the error; a pending image the new card does not own is dropped.</summary>
    /// <param name="value">The card to choose.</param>
    private async Task ApplyChoiceAsync(AvatarChoice value)
    {
        this.choice = value;
        this.error = null;
        if (!this.OwnsImageSlot(value))
        {
            await this.DropPendingAsync();
        }
    }

    /// <summary>Stores the Label box's typed text, once per keystroke; typing chooses the Label card.</summary>
    /// <param name="value">The text now in the box.</param>
    private async Task OnLabelChangedAsync(string value)
    {
        this.label = value;
        await this.ApplyChoiceAsync(AvatarChoice.Label);
        await this.CommitAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>Validates an uploaded image (size, then type) and hands the bytes on; a failure shows the error line and changes nothing.</summary>
    /// <param name="file">The file the Human picked.</param>
    private async Task OnFileChangedAsync(IBrowserFile file)
    {
        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(file);

        this.error = null;

        // Checked before opening the stream at all - fast, and gives a better message than the
        // IOException OpenReadStream's own maxAllowedSize guard would throw for the same file.
        if (file.Size > AvatarImage.MaxBytes)
        {
            this.error = TooLargeMessage();
            return;
        }

        byte[] bytes;
        try
        {
            await using Stream stream = file.OpenReadStream(AvatarImage.MaxBytes, CancellationToken.None);
            using MemoryStream buffer = new();
            await stream.CopyToAsync(buffer, CancellationToken.None);
            bytes = buffer.ToArray();
        }
        catch (IOException)
        {
            // A lying Size (or a stream that grew mid-read) still trips OpenReadStream's own guard - the same fact as
            // the fast check above from the Human's point of view, so the same message.
            this.error = TooLargeMessage();
            return;
        }

        string? extension = AvatarImage.SniffExtension(bytes);
        if (extension is null)
        {
            this.error = "That file is not a PNG, JPEG or WebP image.";
            return;
        }

        await this.TakeImageAsync(bytes, extension, fromLibrary: false);
    }

    /// <summary>The "too large" message, sized from <see cref="AvatarImage.MaxBytes"/>.</summary>
    private static string TooLargeMessage() =>
        string.Create(CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, $"That file is larger than {AvatarImage.MaxBytes / 1000} KB.");

    /// <summary>
    /// Opens the Avatar Library picker. Inside a dialog it replaces this editor's content in place (see the file-level
    /// comment), so the dialog stack stays two deep; elsewhere it is a dialog of its own and, when a thumbnail is chosen,
    /// that file is read and taken as an upload is taken. An unreadable file shows the error line; cancelling changes nothing.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task ChooseFromLibraryAsync()
    {
        this.error = null;

        if (this.Dialog is not null)
        {
            this.libraryOpen = true;
            await this.Dialog.SetOptionsAsync(AvatarLibraryDialog.InlineOptions);
            await this.LibraryOpenChanged.InvokeAsync(true);
            return;
        }

        IDialogReference reference = await this.DialogService.ShowAsync<AvatarLibraryDialog>(null, new DialogParameters(), AvatarLibraryDialog.Options);
        DialogResult? result = await reference.Result;
        if (result is null || result.Canceled || result.Data is not string fileName)
        {
            return;
        }

        await this.TakeLibraryImageAsync(fileName);
    }

    /// <summary>Returns from the library to the editor: the dialog goes back to its own width and the editor's fields are as they were.</summary>
    private async Task CloseLibraryAsync()
    {
        if (!this.libraryOpen)
        {
            return;
        }

        this.libraryOpen = false;
        if (this.Dialog is not null)
        {
            await this.Dialog.SetOptionsAsync(AvatarEditorDialog.Options);
        }

        await this.LibraryOpenChanged.InvokeAsync(false);
    }

    /// <summary>A thumbnail was pressed in the in-place library: go back to the editor and take that picture.</summary>
    /// <param name="fileName">The library file the Human chose.</param>
    private async Task OnLibraryPickedAsync(string fileName)
    {
        await this.CloseLibraryAsync();
        await this.TakeLibraryImageAsync(fileName);
    }

    /// <summary>Reads a library file and takes it as an upload is taken; an unreadable one shows the error line.</summary>
    /// <param name="fileName">The library file the Human chose.</param>
    private async Task TakeLibraryImageAsync(string fileName)
    {
        AvatarLibraryImage? picked = await this.LibraryLoader.ReadImageAsync(fileName, CancellationToken.None);
        if (picked is null)
        {
            this.error = "That image could not be read.";
            return;
        }

        await this.TakeImageAsync(picked.Bytes, picked.Extension, fromLibrary: true);
    }

    /// <summary>Takes a validated image into the single image slot and chooses the card it came from, replacing what the other image card held: written through the store at once in Immediate mode, held as pending in Buffered mode.</summary>
    /// <param name="bytes">The image bytes, already validated as a PNG, JPEG or WebP.</param>
    /// <param name="extension">The extension, with its dot.</param>
    /// <param name="fromLibrary">Whether the picture came from the library card rather than the upload card.</param>
    private async Task TakeImageAsync(byte[] bytes, string extension, bool fromLibrary)
    {
        this.error = null;
        this.imageFromLibrary = fromLibrary;
        this.choice = fromLibrary ? AvatarChoice.Library : AvatarChoice.Upload;
        if (this.SaveMode == AvatarSaveMode.Immediate)
        {
            this.image = this.Avatars.WriteImage(bytes, extension);
        }
        else
        {
            this.pendingBytes = bytes;
            this.pendingExtension = extension;
            await this.PendingImageChanged.InvokeAsync((bytes, extension));
        }

        await this.CommitAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Clears the held image, stored or pending, so the avatar falls back to initials. The upload card stays chosen (it can
    /// be chosen empty); the library card cannot be chosen empty, so removing its picture returns the choice to Initials.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task RemoveImageAsync()
    {
        if (this.choice == AvatarChoice.Library)
        {
            this.choice = AvatarChoice.Initials;
        }

        this.imageFromLibrary = false;
        this.image = null;
        this.error = null;
        await this.DropPendingAsync();
        await this.CommitAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>THE TRAP: the only way <see cref="background"/> gains a colour. Stores the pressed swatch as the six-digit hex the avatar store holds.</summary>
    /// <param name="hex">The pressed swatch's colour, as the six-digit hex the avatar store holds.</param>
    private async Task OnBackgroundPickedAsync(string hex)
    {
        this.background = hex;
        this.error = null;
        await this.CommitAsync();
    }

    /// <summary>Clears the background back to the theme's own colour.</summary>
    private async Task UseThemeColourAsync()
    {
        this.background = null;
        this.error = null;
        await this.CommitAsync();
    }
}
